-- Inaccessible patterns — the dot — MS9 phase 228.
--
-- When a split determines one of a constructor's arguments, that argument has
-- no binder left in the case it produces. Splitting a `Vec A (s n)` makes
-- `vcons`'s own length equal to `n`, so the case binds two arguments and not
-- three.
--
-- Thena lets you write THREE things in such a position, and all three are
-- legal here on purpose:
--
--   * a NAME, which is bound as a definition equal to the term the position
--     was determined to. `k = n` is then in the context and `refl` proves
--     `k = n`, the equality being definitional.
--   * `_`, which asks for nothing at all.
--   * a DOT, `.n` or `.(s n)`, which binds nothing and ASSERTS that the
--     position is determined and by what. It is checked: the written term is
--     elaborated at the type the position has and unified with the term the
--     equation forced.
--
-- The dot is OPTIONAL and can never be made mandatory — his ruling of
-- 2026-10-19. Agda demands it to keep a left-hand side linear so that a
-- matcher can run; Thena elaborates to an eliminator and has no left-hand side
-- to keep linear, so the constraint that forces Agda's hand does not reach
-- here. What a dot buys is a CHECK: a name means a binder or a definition
-- depending on a unification you cannot see, and a dot says which you expected.
--
-- `DECISIONS.md`, *Dot patterns are optional here*, has the whole argument.

module DotPatterns where

data N : Type₀ where
  z : N
  s : N -> N

data Vec (A : Type) : N -> Type where
  vnil : Vec A z
  vcons : forall (n : N) (a : A) (as : Vec A n) -> Vec A (s n)

-- The forced position written as a dot. `vcons`'s `n` is determined to be `m`,
-- because the target's index is `s m` and `vcons`'s conclusion is `s n`.
vtailDotted : forall (A : Type₀) (m : N) (xs : Vec A (s m)) -> Vec A m
vtailDotted = \ A m xs -> case xs of { vnil -> ; vcons .m a as -> as }

-- The same proof with the position NAMED, which is what the ruling keeps
-- working. Nothing here is second-class: this is the spelling a user who has
-- never heard of an inaccessible pattern writes.
vtailNamed : forall (A : Type₀) (m : N) (xs : Vec A (s m)) -> Vec A m
vtailNamed = \ A m xs -> case xs of { vnil -> ; vcons n a as -> as }

-- And with `_`, which asks for no name.
vtailAnon : forall (A : Type₀) (m : N) (xs : Vec A (s m)) -> Vec A m
vtailAnon = \ A m xs -> case xs of { vnil -> ; vcons _ a as -> as }

-- A position forced to a COMPOUND term needs the parentheses, and the written
-- term is an ordinary term: splitting a `Vec A (s (s m))` forces `vcons`'s `n`
-- to `s m`.
vtailTwo : forall (A : Type₀) (m : N) (xs : Vec A (s (s m))) -> Vec A (s m)
vtailTwo = \ A m xs -> case xs of { vnil -> ; vcons .(s m) a as -> as }

-- `._` is the dot's own placeholder: it asserts the position is determined and
-- declines to say by what. A placeholder elaborates to a hole and unification
-- solves it, so this costs nothing beyond the assertion.
vtailDotAnon : forall (A : Type₀) (m : N) (xs : Vec A (s m)) -> Vec A m
vtailDotAnon = \ A m xs -> case xs of { vnil -> ; vcons ._ a as -> as }

-- A split that forces nothing. `len`'s target is `Vec A m` with `m` a plain
-- variable, so the split generalises it and `vcons`'s own `n` SURVIVES as a
-- binder. Writing a dot there is refused — that is the whole of what the
-- notation buys, and the two lines below are the illegal ones:
--
--   len = \ A m xs -> induction xs of
--           { vnil -> z ; vcons .m a as -> s m }
--
-- refused: no clause of dotted-position-is-forced applies here
--
-- and a dot whose term is not the one the equation forced:
--
--   vtailDotted = \ A m xs -> case xs of
--                   { vnil -> ; vcons .(s m) a as -> as }
--
-- refused: s m and m cannot be made equal
len : forall (A : Type₀) (m : N) (xs : Vec A m) -> N
len = \ A m xs -> induction xs of { vnil -> z ; vcons n a as -> s (len A n as) }

-- The dot is checked at the position's TYPE as well as its value, so a term of
-- the wrong type is refused before the unification is reached:
--
--   vcons .A a as -> as    refused: Type₀ and N cannot be made equal
--
-- A closed value, so the whole file really computes.
two : N
two = len N (s z) (vcons N z z (vnil N))
